@model DualPath.Web.Pages.IndexModel
<div class="wrap content-width"><div class="page-intro"><div class="eyebrow">Clear expectations</div><h1>@(Model.Section=="privacy"?"Your work deserves thoughtful handling.":"A practical service. Clear boundaries.")</h1></div><section class="card prose">
@if(Model.Section=="privacy"){
<h3>What is saved</h3><p>Your account details, learning goals, assessment attempts, completed lessons, submitted work, reflections, feedback, memberships, notifications, and support requests are saved to operate the service. Payment card details are handled by the payment provider, not this application.</p><h3>Who can see your learning</h3><p>You can access your own records. Your assigned instructor can review work and reflections associated with their cohort. Institution administrators manage memberships, cohorts and programme reports. Platform administration is permissioned and audited.</p><h3>AI practice is optional</h3><p>AI practice requires an explicit choice in account settings. It sends the selected assessment question and the practice answer you submit to the configured AI processor. Your reflections, email address and account profile are not included in that request. AI responses are not instructor grades.</p><h3>Your controls</h3><p>Manage notification preferences and AI consent in your account. Download your own learning records there. To request correction or deletion, open a support request. The operator must assess applicable retention and institutional requirements before deleting records.</p><h3>Service cookies and retention</h3><p>Essential session and antiforgery cookies keep sign-in and form actions secure. The deployment operator is responsible for publishing its identity, contact details, processing regions, legal basis, retention schedule, and third-party processor details before admitting production customers.</p>
}else{
<h3>What DualPath provides</h3><p>Structured internship preparation, practical exercises, learning records and feedback through the programme you join. DualPath does not guarantee employment, admission, compensation or an internship.</p><h3>Accounts and original work</h3><p>Keep account access private, provide accurate details, and submit work you are entitled to share. Do not upload confidential third-party information or harmful files. Staff must use their assigned access for legitimate programme operations.</p><h3>Plans and cancellation</h3><p>A paid plan starts only through the configured secure checkout. Its price, currency, billing interval and applicable terms must be shown before payment. Use your billing portal to review cancellation and subscription changes. Institutional access also depends on authorised membership and seat availability.</p><h3>Questions and disputes</h3><p>Open a support request for access, billing, content or privacy concerns. Before commercial launch, the operator must publish its legal identity, jurisdiction, support contact, refund rules and any age/guardian requirements that apply to its customers.</p>
}
</section></div>
